WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.240
CARTER MORGAN: Today we're
talking about Cloud Spanner

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.080
ecosystem restoration and
Chrome browser Cloud Management.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.690
I'm Carter Morgan, and welcome
to "This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:12.450
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.480
Cloud Spanner is a fully
managed relational database

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.120
with unlimited scale,
strong consistency,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.790
and up to five nines
of availability.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.280
To achieve the best
performance characteristics,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.220
it's advisable to launch your
production application when

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:29.160
Spanner is in a warm state
with splits already balanced

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.500
across all of the
server resources.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.280
Check out the blog for
a step-by-step resource.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.310
Protecting the Earth's ecosystem
from further degradation

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:41.010
and improving outcomes for
the wildlife and communities

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.040
that rely on them needs to be
a focus for the next decade

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.330
of climate action.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:46.980
But where do we start?

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.680
Head to the blog to learn more
about how Restore is helping

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.830
to solve for knowledge gaps
and accelerate restoration

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.650
with data.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:57.020
IT and security teams have
a lot on their plate--

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.510
from supporting the transition
to new work environments

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.330
to preventing an increasing
number of security attacks--

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.700
and as more and more work
is done in the browser,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.430
it's important for IT and
security professionals

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.410
to look at the browser
as a critical piece

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.250
of infrastructure to keep
their organization secure.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.950
Chrome Browser Cloud
Management gives IT teams

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.040
a simple and efficient
way to manage and secure

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.710
their browser across
multiple operating systems,

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.090
all from the Cloud.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.597
Check out the link for examples.

00:01:25.597 --> 00:01:27.680
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:30.027
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:30.027 --> 00:01:31.610
And if you have any
thoughts or ideas,

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.480
leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.770
We'll see you in the Cloud.

